.TH ZDOTS-GRAPH-AUDIT 1 "2026-07-21" "zdots" "zdots manual"
.SH NAME
zdots-graph-audit \- bin/zdots\-graph\-audit — assert zdots' code\-graph security invariants hold.
.SH SYNOPSIS
See OPTIONS below (generated from \fBzdots-graph-audit --help\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
bin/zdots-graph-audit — assert zdots' code-graph security invariants hold.

A graph-based contract test over the Ruby in lib/zdots/ (the part of zdots that
graphify reads accurately): the local-AI/PHI gate and the encryption key store.
It encodes "every inference path routes through assert_local!" and "encrypted
attributes go through the key store" as queries against graphify's graph, so a
refactor that quietly bypasses a boundary fails the check. Also summarizes the
exposed capability surface (bin/ entrypoints + env requirements).

Local-only, no LLM. Exit 0 if all invariants hold; exit 1 on any violation.
CI-friendly: run after changes under lib/zdots/.

Usage: zdots-graph-audit [--no-build] [-h|--help]
.fi
